Give it a shot.

259
00:13:44,181 --> 00:13:46,321
If it's too scary, we can switch.

260
00:13:49,121 --> 00:13:50,890
Good job driving all the way here.

261
00:13:50,891 --> 00:13:51,960
Good job.

262
00:13:51,961 --> 00:13:55,531
(Lodging, Ramen restaurant)

263
00:13:59,571 --> 00:14:00,800
Let's go.

264
00:14:00,801 --> 00:14:03,240
- Let's go eat ramen finally.
- Judging...

265
00:14:03,241 --> 00:14:05,340
by all of the cars coming
in, I do think it's a good place.

266
00:14:05,341 --> 00:14:06,570
They're really pouring in.

267
00:14:06,571 --> 00:14:08,140
We need to hurry inside and eat.

268
00:14:08,141 --> 00:14:10,340
They open at 11am, and it's 4 minutes past.

269
00:14:10,341 --> 00:14:11,750
Oh, it hasn't been too
long since they opened.

270
00:14:11,751 --> 00:14:12,781
That's right.

271
00:14:13,111 --> 00:14:14,351
(Oh, my.)

272
00:14:14,781 --> 00:14:15,781
I like the vibe.

273
00:14:15,782 --> 00:14:16,920
Cool summer.

274
00:14:16,921 --> 00:14:17,990
(You can already tell it's
a great local restaurant.)

275
00:14:17,991 --> 00:14:20,151
I think they have cold ramen too.

276
00:14:20,821 --> 00:14:21,821
Oh, cold ramen.

277
00:14:21,822 --> 00:14:22,921
I'm hungry.

278
00:14:23,621 --> 00:14:26,031
- Hello.
- Hello.

279
00:14:26,231 --> 00:14:28,301
- Hello.
- We should sit like this, right?

280
00:14:28,561 --> 00:14:30,031
We have three people.

281
00:14:30,301 --> 00:14:31,500
Are all three of you eating?

282
00:14:31,501 --> 00:14:32,531
Yes.

283
00:14:32,671 --> 00:14:34,440
- Let's sit here.
- Right, we can sit here.

284
00:14:34,441 --> 00:14:37,171
(They successfully got seats
at a popular Tokushima spot.)

285
00:14:37,711 --> 00:14:39,141
I'll use Papago.

286
00:14:39,271 --> 00:14:40,841
Ramen with meat.

287
00:14:42,181 --> 00:14:43,781
Salt ramen with meat.

288
00:14:44,111 --> 00:14:45,310
Veggie ramen with meat.

289
00:14:45,311 --> 00:14:46,410
That's the most popular one.

290
00:14:46,411 --> 00:14:48,021
Japanese style...

291
00:14:50,551 --> 00:14:52,251
Oh, the owner looks so cool.

292
00:14:53,221 --> 00:14:54,720
He's even wearing earrings.

293
00:14:54,721 --> 00:14:55,721
He's a cool guy.

294
00:15:06,271 --> 00:15:08,841
This place is about 15
minutes from the city center.

295
00:15:09,071 --> 00:15:10,600
There are no tourists here.

296
00:15:10,601 --> 00:15:12,341
Of course, there's no Korean.

297
00:15:12,571 --> 00:15:14,011
It's a totally local spot.

298
00:15:15,841 --> 00:15:19,751
(Tokushima ramen served by the cool owner)

299
00:15:20,651 --> 00:15:23,951
(It's only available for four
hours, from 11am to 3pm.)

300
00:15:25,121 --> 00:15:29,891
(A hidden ramen spot in
Tokushima loved by locals)

301
00:15:30,161 --> 00:15:34,361
Tokushima ramen already
has soft-boiled egg added.

302
00:15:35,101 --> 00:15:38,200
You can also choose to
dip noodles in raw egg.

303
00:15:38,201 --> 00:15:39,370
Because it can be a bit salty.

304
00:15:39,371 --> 00:15:41,601
- Tsukemen?
- Yes. So it's good to order this.

305
00:15:41,841 --> 00:15:42,940
Raw egg.

306
00:15:42,941 --> 00:15:44,571
(Hyun Moo suggests adding a raw egg.)

307
00:15:45,011 --> 00:15:48,140
What do you want to eat?
Veggie ramen with meat?

308
00:15:48,141 --> 00:15:49,710
- Veggie ramen with meat.
- Veggie ramen with meat.

309
00:15:49,711 --> 00:15:50,981
Veggie ramen with meat?

310
00:15:51,611 --> 00:15:52,811
Excuse me.

311
00:15:53,151 --> 00:15:55,550
(Their order, 3 veggie ramen with meat)

312
00:15:55,551 --> 00:15:56,951
(3 raw eggs)

313
00:15:57,251 --> 00:15:58,521
(Order received.)

314
00:16:04,631 --> 00:16:07,931
(Moving his body to the
music playing in the restaurant)

315
00:16:08,701 --> 00:16:11,000
How do you remember
all of those songs, Joon?

316
00:16:11,001 --> 00:16:12,961
They were promoting their
music at the same time.

317
00:16:13,201 --> 00:16:14,470
It's not that I memorized them.

318
00:16:14,471 --> 00:16:15,940
I think they just stayed with me naturally.

319
00:16:15,941 --> 00:16:17,340
- I always saw them on music shows.
- Right.

320
00:16:17,341 --> 00:16:19,841
That makes sense. At rehearsals too.

321
00:16:22,381 --> 00:16:23,741
Oh, my.

322
00:16:24,481 --> 00:16:25,910
- Oh, my. This is...
- Oh, my.

323
00:16:25,911 --> 00:16:27,480
(They can't help but exclaim
at how appetizing it looks.)

324
00:16:27,481 --> 00:16:28,550
Apparently, that's the most popular one.

325
00:16:28,551 --> 00:16:30,281
It looks so great.

326
00:16:32,991 --> 00:16:34,590
What's with the egg?

327
00:16:34,591 --> 00:16:35,921
Dip it in the raw egg.

328
00:16:36,191 --> 00:16:37,320
- Dip what?
- The noodles.

329
00:16:37,321 --> 00:16:38,561
Oh, really?

330
00:16:39,591 --> 00:16:40,830
(Tokushima ramen, Traditional ramen
of Tokushima Prefecture, Shikoku)

331
00:16:40,831 --> 00:16:41,960
Cabbage.

332
00:16:41,961 --> 00:16:43,130
It's a bit new. It's different, right?

333
00:16:43,131 --> 00:16:45,271
(The raw egg dip makes it unique.)

334
00:16:45,671 --> 00:16:47,901
It's so unique. Tokushima
ramen uses pork belly.

335
00:16:52,541 --> 00:16:55,911
(Rich broth and various toppings)

336
00:16:56,941 --> 00:17:01,011
(Veggie ramen with meat,
Traditional Tokushima style)

337
00:17:01,111 --> 00:17:02,631
It reminds me of "Cooking Master Boy."

338
00:17:05,751 --> 00:17:08,491
(Something out of a cooking manga)

339
00:17:13,161 --> 00:17:14,290
- What is this?
- A whole slab of pork belly!

340
00:17:14,291 --> 00:17:16,460
- Do you like the soup?
- I do.

341
00:17:16,461 --> 00:17:17,561
I'm going crazy.

342
00:17:20,171 --> 00:17:22,971
(Insanely delicious)

343
00:17:28,441 --> 00:17:30,310
(Oh, my...)

344
00:17:30,311 --> 00:17:31,411
It's good.

345
00:17:36,021 --> 00:17:37,821
- It's not salty at all.
- Is it a miso base?

346
00:17:40,621 --> 00:17:43,190
(A soup made with rich pork bone broth, )

347
00:17:43,191 --> 00:17:46,231
(soy sauce, and vegetables)

348
00:17:47,131 --> 00:17:50,401
(Tokushima ramen has a
delicious rich and deep flavour.)

349
00:17:50,801 --> 00:17:52,731
The raw egg is so fun.

350
00:17:57,201 --> 00:18:01,041
(Nam Gil is more serious than ever.)

351
00:18:22,231 --> 00:18:23,661
Oh, this is good.

352
00:18:24,971 --> 00:18:27,201
Hey, Nam Gil. Are you happy?

353
00:18:27,371 --> 00:18:29,071
I'm so happy right now.

354
00:18:30,501 --> 00:18:31,571
This is insane.

355
00:18:34,841 --> 00:18:36,481
The thing Nam Gil wanted to eat the most.

356
00:18:36,881 --> 00:18:38,201
You're finally getting to eat it.

357
00:18:50,221 --> 00:18:51,490
- Is it good?
- I've never had ramen...

358
00:18:51,491 --> 00:18:52,961
- that I dip in raw egg.
- Right.

359
00:18:53,761 --> 00:18:54,931
It's really delicious.

360
00:19:01,871 --> 00:19:03,900
(Scrunching his face
out of satisfaction again)

361
00:19:03,901 --> 00:19:04,971
They're good.

362
00:19:05,241 --> 00:19:07,521
It really would've been sad
if we didn't get the raw egg.

363
00:19:07,641 --> 00:19:09,981
Is dipping ramen noodles in raw egg...

364
00:19:10,581 --> 00:19:11,980
unique to this place?
I've never seen it before.

365
00:19:11,981 --> 00:19:12,981
Me too.

366
00:19:12,982 --> 00:19:14,480
Is it just in Tokushima?

367
00:19:14,481 --> 00:19:16,820
It's their style. The raw egg.

368
00:19:16,821 --> 00:19:17,821
(Tokushima is most well-known
for having raw egg with ramen, )

369
00:19:17,821 --> 00:19:18,821
(but other regions in Japan
eat ramen with raw egg too.)

370
00:19:18,822 --> 00:19:21,051
This is really nice,
dipping noodles in raw egg.

371
00:19:21,821 --> 00:19:23,360
(Ramen and raw egg)

372
00:19:23,361 --> 00:19:24,790
(Flavours of the rich soup
and the salty meat...)

373
00:19:24,791 --> 00:19:27,631
(blend with the raw egg to
create a sukiyaki-like feel.)

374
00:19:40,811 --> 00:19:42,780
(A colourful dish that's
a joy for the mouth)

375
00:19:42,781 --> 00:19:45,111
I love this type of ramen.

376
00:19:45,951 --> 00:19:47,011
Oh, my.

377
00:19:49,581 --> 00:19:52,421
(Oh, yes!)

378
00:19:54,051 --> 00:19:56,120
(Thanks to the added
smokiness from the torching, )

379
00:19:56,121 --> 00:19:58,861
(the chashu is extra aromatic.)

380
00:20:05,331 --> 00:20:07,070
The meat is so tender.

381
00:20:07,071 --> 00:20:08,101
Isn't it amazing?

382
00:20:09,641 --> 00:20:11,511
- It bites off so easily.
- You're right.

383
00:20:11,971 --> 00:20:13,371
- Why is it so tender?
- So tender.

384
00:20:16,311 --> 00:20:19,081
(They can't stop exclaiming
at how tender the chashu is.)

385
00:20:19,151 --> 00:20:21,271
How did they boil the pork
belly to get it so tender?

386
00:20:22,981 --> 00:20:24,720
It's thick but tender, right?

387
00:20:24,721 --> 00:20:25,791
Yes.

388
00:20:37,231 --> 00:20:38,601
The meat is so... Oh, my.

389
00:20:40,031 --> 00:20:41,670
You've had a lot of
other ramen before, right?

390
00:20:41,671 --> 00:20:43,617
- I've had a lot.
- What do you think of this place?

391
00:20:43,641 --> 00:20:45,940
- It's different. It's very unique.
- It's unique, right?

392
00:20:45,941 --> 00:20:47,170
It's very unique,

393
00:20:47,171 --> 00:20:49,040
but it doesn't mean it tastes weird.

394
00:20:49,041 --> 00:20:51,087
It's not a flavour some would
love and some would hate.

395
00:20:51,111 --> 00:20:52,481
It's very delicious.

396
00:20:52,711 --> 00:20:54,720
And the cabbage doesn't
seem so important, but...

397
00:20:54,721 --> 00:20:55,950
- It's good, right?
- Yes.

398
00:20:55,951 --> 00:20:57,181
It has a sweetness, right?

399
00:20:57,551 --> 00:21:00,490
The cabbage also adds an
interesting layer of texture.

400
00:21:00,491 --> 00:21:02,060
(The cabbage adds a crunchy
texture and a sweetness to the ramen.)

401
00:21:02,061 --> 00:21:03,861
The napa cabbage is so good.

402
00:21:06,231 --> 00:21:07,330
Oh, goodness.

403
00:21:07,331 --> 00:21:08,561
(Intensely moved)

404
00:21:19,641 --> 00:21:20,811
Cold noodles.

405
00:21:23,581 --> 00:21:26,281
(Moo Friends, doesn't this look good?)

406
00:21:35,591 --> 00:21:37,591
(Oh, my.)

407
00:21:43,831 --> 00:21:46,471
Tokushima ramen can be a bit salty.

408
00:21:46,771 --> 00:21:49,170
So I used to always order
rice and add it to the soup.

409
00:21:49,171 --> 00:21:50,641
But this place isn't like that.

410
00:21:51,611 --> 00:21:54,111
- Delicious.
- The napa cabbage is so good.

411
00:22:17,561 --> 00:22:18,771
Oh, this ramen is good.

412
00:22:19,131 --> 00:22:21,071
The soup is a bit different
from what we have.

413
00:22:21,271 --> 00:22:22,271
Right.

414
00:22:22,272 --> 00:22:24,811
(The three brothers are in
love with Tokushima ramen.)

415
00:22:31,681 --> 00:22:32,681
(Sighing contentedly)

416
00:22:35,421 --> 00:22:37,081
I finally granted Nam Gil's wish.

417
00:22:37,721 --> 00:22:39,867
I guessed you'd keep talking
about it if we didn't have this.

418
00:22:39,891 --> 00:22:41,331
Should we have ramen for dinner too?

419
00:22:41,391 --> 00:22:42,421
We have to.

420
00:22:43,591 --> 00:22:44,891
We can just eat noodles.

421
00:22:46,731 --> 00:22:47,861
It's delicious.

422
00:22:48,661 --> 00:22:50,701
(Thank you.)

423
00:22:50,931 --> 00:22:52,430
It was very delicious.

424
00:22:52,431 --> 00:22:53,631
Thank you for the meal.

425
00:22:54,701 --> 00:22:56,741
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

426
00:22:58,911 --> 00:23:00,811
I've prepared something. Let's go.

427
00:23:04,441 --> 00:23:05,751
I think we're very high up.

428
00:23:06,381 --> 00:23:08,981
The trees are so high. So long.

429
00:23:09,651 --> 00:23:11,050
They have to be.

430
00:23:11,051 --> 00:23:12,450
- Oh, really?
- What is it?

431
00:23:12,451 --> 00:23:14,391
It's not fun if it's not high.

432
00:23:15,391 --> 00:23:17,290
Do you still not know?

433
00:23:17,291 --> 00:23:18,491
What is this?

434
00:23:19,131 --> 00:23:21,230
- Where are we?
- The Alps.

435
00:23:21,231 --> 00:23:22,261
(Ramen restaurant)

436
00:23:22,401 --> 00:23:23,530
The Alps of Japan.

437
00:23:23,531 --> 00:23:24,561
(What is this place?)

438
00:23:26,201 --> 00:23:29,301
(Iya Valley, one of Japan's
Top 3 most beautiful sights)

439
00:23:30,541 --> 00:23:33,841
(Follow the jade-coloured
water flowing down the valley, )

440
00:23:36,181 --> 00:23:39,451
(and you'll find Hinoji Valley,
in the shape of the letter "Hi.")

441
00:23:41,151 --> 00:23:42,780
(Iya Valley Point 2)

442
00:23:42,781 --> 00:23:44,981
(The Statue of a Peeing Boy
standing alone at the edge)

443
00:23:45,021 --> 00:23:46,720
(Iya Valley Point 3)

444
00:23:46,721 --> 00:23:48,861
(Iya Vine Bridge, made
with 6 tons of vines)

445
00:23:50,161 --> 00:23:53,060
(Iya Valley Point 4)

446
00:23:53,061 --> 00:23:55,561
(Oboke Gorge, a rafting mecca)

447
00:23:57,531 --> 00:24:00,731
(Tokushima Trip, All-in-one Mother Nature)

448
00:24:01,841 --> 00:24:03,200
The electrical wires... What is this?

449
00:24:03,201 --> 00:24:04,201
(What is this?)

450
00:24:05,771 --> 00:24:06,811
What?

451
00:24:07,641 --> 00:24:08,841
Is it good or not?

452
00:24:09,711 --> 00:24:11,311
It's a zipline.

453
00:24:11,881 --> 00:24:13,250
- This is fun.
- It is.

454
00:24:13,251 --> 00:24:14,681
We can handle ziplines.

455
00:24:16,521 --> 00:24:20,291
(A zipline in the lush forest that
looks like something out of a movie)

456
00:24:21,861 --> 00:24:26,491
(Height of 50m, length of 360m)

457
00:24:27,531 --> 00:24:29,130
(An extreme activity...)

458
00:24:29,131 --> 00:24:31,971
(that goes across the gorge)

459
00:24:33,531 --> 00:24:38,311
(You can enjoy both the
thrill of flying through the sky...)

460
00:24:38,671 --> 00:24:40,470
(and the beautiful nature at
this hidden Tokushima spot.)

461
00:24:40,471 --> 00:24:42,711
(You can do it here! The perfect thrill!)

462
00:24:43,211 --> 00:24:44,440
(Shouting, Surprised)

463
00:24:44,441 --> 00:24:47,150
- There. The zipline.
- Oh, it's high.

464
00:24:47,151 --> 00:24:49,351
Is there a net below? There isn't.

465
00:24:51,151 --> 00:24:53,121
They're shouting so much.

466
00:24:54,291 --> 00:24:56,361
- It's very fast.
- It looks unreal.

467
00:24:56,491 --> 00:24:57,691
Why is he going backwards?

468
00:24:58,161 --> 00:25:00,521
I've done many ziplines, but
I've never seen one that fast.

469
00:25:00,831 --> 00:25:02,760
Oh, wait.

470
00:25:02,761 --> 00:25:04,001
Isn't that person injured?

471
00:25:04,801 --> 00:25:06,970
You can just land on your feet.

472
00:25:06,971 --> 00:25:08,071
What if I break my feet?

473
00:25:09,701 --> 00:25:13,171
(Oinouchi, Nishiiyayama,
Miyoshi, Tokushima Prefecture)

474
00:25:14,541 --> 00:25:16,641
Do we get instructions? We do.

475
00:25:16,741 --> 00:25:18,211
Hello.

476
00:25:18,951 --> 00:25:21,111
- Zipline.
- Zipline.

477
00:25:21,951 --> 00:25:24,220
(Zipline: 2,500 yen, gloves: 300 yen)

478
00:25:24,221 --> 00:25:26,491
(Total: approximately
25 dollars per person)

479
00:25:27,191 --> 00:25:29,521
- Let's get your harness on.
- Okay.

480
00:25:33,231 --> 00:25:34,591
Pull it up to your waist.

481
00:25:37,631 --> 00:25:38,700
Up.

482
00:25:38,701 --> 00:25:39,800
That's where you hold?

483
00:25:39,801 --> 00:25:42,601
(After putting on the safety gear
and completing the safety briefing, )

484
00:25:43,041 --> 00:25:44,270
- Okay!
- Okay.

485
00:25:44,271 --> 00:25:46,210
(they brace themselves
and head to the zipline.)

486
00:25:46,211 --> 00:25:49,641
This is the fun kind of thrill.

487
00:25:49,841 --> 00:25:52,180
I hate going vertically.

488
00:25:52,181 --> 00:25:54,210
- Me too.
- I like going horizontally.

489
00:25:54,211 --> 00:25:55,351
Me too.

490
00:25:56,351 --> 00:25:57,720
Imagine you have to jump from this.

491
00:25:57,721 --> 00:25:59,891
Gosh, hey! Come here.

492
00:26:00,221 --> 00:26:01,697
It's like standing here without this.

493
00:26:01,721 --> 00:26:02,861
Could you jump?

494
00:26:03,691 --> 00:26:04,760
(A dizzying height, even at a glance)

495
00:26:04,761 --> 00:26:06,961
No. Why would I do that?

496
00:26:07,161 --> 00:26:08,331
I can't jump.

497
00:26:08,801 --> 00:26:10,231
I could never jump from here.

498
00:26:10,461 --> 00:26:13,171
It's just horrible.

499
00:26:14,001 --> 00:26:15,601
Bungee jumping is even higher than this.

500
00:26:15,871 --> 00:26:17,870
- It's way higher.
- It's way higher.

501
00:26:17,871 --> 00:26:19,631
(The three brothers
are chattier than ever.)

502
00:26:19,771 --> 00:26:20,911
Goodness.

503
00:26:21,611 --> 00:26:23,541
The nature here is crazy.

504
00:26:23,881 --> 00:26:25,451
Amazing.

505
00:26:25,651 --> 00:26:26,680
It's an amazing nature.

506
00:26:26,681 --> 00:26:28,251
What trees are those?

507
00:26:30,021 --> 00:26:31,320
They have long legs.

508
00:26:31,321 --> 00:26:32,620
(A whole forest of tall, leggy cedars)

509
00:26:32,621 --> 00:26:33,981
Right. They have really long legs.

510
00:26:35,461 --> 00:26:37,891
- The smell of the mountain.
- Why?

511
00:26:38,091 --> 00:26:39,831
The smell of the mountain and grass.

512
00:26:40,591 --> 00:26:41,660
Phytoncides.

513
00:26:41,661 --> 00:26:42,961
The smell of phytoncides.

514
00:26:43,861 --> 00:26:46,631
(Refreshing phytoncides
that clear your mind)

515
00:26:46,971 --> 00:26:49,740
(Smacking)

516
00:26:49,741 --> 00:26:52,640
There's a baby video...

517
00:26:52,641 --> 00:26:54,840
where the camera is this close here,

518
00:26:54,841 --> 00:26:57,340
filming a baby eating.

519
00:26:57,341 --> 00:26:58,481
- With this?
- Yes.

520
00:26:58,851 --> 00:26:59,951
It looks like that.

521
00:27:01,351 --> 00:27:04,821
(The viral eating show
with 5.6 million views)

522
00:27:05,521 --> 00:27:06,820
(He attempts to film a
phytoncides eating show...)

523
00:27:06,821 --> 00:27:08,121
(aiming for 5 million views.)

524
00:27:08,961 --> 00:27:10,021
It's this place?

525
00:27:11,831 --> 00:27:12,961
It's up there.

526
00:27:15,161 --> 00:27:19,500
(The zip line launch point lies
beyond an aerial obstacle course.)

527
00:27:19,501 --> 00:27:23,741
(Zipline starting point, landing point 1)

528
00:27:24,341 --> 00:27:26,740
(50m above the ground and 360m long)

529
00:27:26,741 --> 00:27:29,881
(A ride through nature)

530
00:27:31,411 --> 00:27:34,350
(They must wear their own
safety gear throughout the course.)

531
00:27:34,351 --> 00:27:36,821
(Zipline landing point 1, landing point 2)

532
00:27:36,981 --> 00:27:39,101
(They'll take the second
zipline to landing point 2.)

533
00:27:39,351 --> 00:27:41,251
(A round-trip course
with two rides in total)

534
00:27:41,651 --> 00:27:43,460
(Easy, right?)

535
00:27:43,461 --> 00:27:44,521
First person.

536
00:27:44,691 --> 00:27:45,791
Who'll go first?

537
00:27:46,531 --> 00:27:47,661
- Kim Nam Gil.
- Number two.

538
00:27:48,961 --> 00:27:50,730
- Go, Nam Gil.
- Okay.

539
00:27:50,731 --> 00:27:52,430
Nam Gil, Lee Joon, Jun Hyun Moo.

540
00:27:52,431 --> 00:27:53,431
Okay.

541
00:27:54,131 --> 00:27:56,370
Why do I want to pee now?

542
00:27:56,371 --> 00:27:58,691
(The eldest is having bladder
issues from all the nerves.)

543
00:28:00,811 --> 00:28:01,880
Okay, go on.

544
00:28:01,881 --> 00:28:02,881
Okay.

545
00:28:03,141 --> 00:28:04,541
Mr. Nam Gil!

546
00:28:05,041 --> 00:28:06,050
Yes.

547
00:28:06,051 --> 00:28:08,150
(Walking)

548
00:28:08,151 --> 00:28:09,381
Mr. Nam Gil!

549
00:28:11,251 --> 00:28:12,721
He's going up like a mackerel.

550
00:28:15,161 --> 00:28:20,761
(The youngest also joins
the line of mackerels.)

551
00:28:21,491 --> 00:28:22,601
Is it hard?

552
00:28:23,361 --> 00:28:24,531
It's a bit scary.

553
00:28:24,901 --> 00:28:26,531
It's scary? This is scary?

554
00:28:26,631 --> 00:28:27,771
A bit.

555
00:28:28,171 --> 00:28:29,241
Okay.

556
00:28:31,941 --> 00:28:34,011
This is scary.

557
00:28:36,581 --> 00:28:38,241
This is really scary.

558
00:28:38,681 --> 00:28:40,810
- It's scary, isn't it?
- This is scary.

559
00:28:40,811 --> 00:28:41,951
See?

560
00:28:42,981 --> 00:28:44,141
You can't say it's not scary.

561
00:28:44,721 --> 00:28:46,291
It's like walking in the sky.

562
00:28:46,651 --> 00:28:47,851
This is really scary.

563
00:28:48,391 --> 00:28:49,761
It's even scarier up here.

564
00:28:50,321 --> 00:28:51,461
It's higher than you think.

565
00:28:53,091 --> 00:28:54,691
There's nothing on my back.

566
00:28:57,161 --> 00:28:58,531
This is my point of view.

567
00:28:58,901 --> 00:28:59,930
This.

568
00:28:59,931 --> 00:29:02,340
This... How are we supposed to go there?

569
00:29:02,341 --> 00:29:03,471
It's scary, right?

570
00:29:03,941 --> 00:29:05,141
There's a net.

571
00:29:05,571 --> 00:29:06,711
It's higher than I thought.

572
00:29:08,141 --> 00:29:09,680
People watching this wouldn't be scared,

573
00:29:09,681 --> 00:29:11,981
but it's really frightening
for people standing here.

574
00:29:13,551 --> 00:29:15,621
Can you go through these stairs?

575
00:29:15,851 --> 00:29:17,621
I think you can just cross it.

576
00:29:18,791 --> 00:29:20,351
That's how you're supposed to go?

577
00:29:21,421 --> 00:29:27,331
(The second brother, an action
pro, goes ahead with confidence.)

578
00:29:29,131 --> 00:29:31,211
I thought I was supposed
to step on the wooden part.

579
00:29:33,631 --> 00:29:36,231
- This is scarier than I thought.
- It's so scary. I want to pee.

580
00:29:36,871 --> 00:29:38,540
Why are we getting scared of a zipline?

581
00:29:38,541 --> 00:29:40,671
- This is crazy.
- Ziplines...

582
00:29:41,141 --> 00:29:43,841
aren't supposed to be
scary. Getting there is scary.

583
00:29:44,341 --> 00:29:45,410
Go?

584
00:29:45,411 --> 00:29:49,251
(They're both action stars,
but they seem different.)

585
00:29:56,921 --> 00:29:58,221
It's scary!

586
00:29:59,531 --> 00:30:00,591
Goodness.

587
00:30:01,931 --> 00:30:03,460
Why is this scary? I can't believe it.

588
00:30:03,461 --> 00:30:04,561
It's annoying!

589
00:30:04,831 --> 00:30:06,031
It's scary!

590
00:30:06,831 --> 00:30:08,071
Why is this scary?

591
00:30:09,401 --> 00:30:11,501
(Feeling calm)

592
00:30:13,071 --> 00:30:14,471
Are you scared Nam Gil?

593
00:30:15,681 --> 00:30:18,011
(I'm even more scared.)

594
00:30:18,411 --> 00:30:21,111
(Unshaken and calm)

595
00:30:21,711 --> 00:30:23,080
- Isn't it scary?
- I'll get going.

596
00:30:23,081 --> 00:30:24,121
Awesome!

597
00:30:24,681 --> 00:30:26,090
- Isn't it scary?
- I'll get going.

598
00:30:26,091 --> 00:30:27,151
Awesome!

599
00:30:28,051 --> 00:30:29,561
(That's how it goes?)

600
00:30:29,761 --> 00:30:31,160
- Isn't it scary?
- I'll get going.

601
00:30:31,161 --> 00:30:32,191
Awesome!

602
00:30:33,061 --> 00:30:34,131
Amazing!

603
00:30:34,991 --> 00:30:37,731
(The second brother
glides through the air.)

604
00:30:40,531 --> 00:30:41,531
Bye!

605
00:30:41,532 --> 00:30:42,572
(What's scary about this?)

606
00:30:44,071 --> 00:30:46,471
(A thrilling glide through the
air with no safety net below)

607
00:30:46,911 --> 00:30:48,011
Why is it going so far?

608
00:30:49,281 --> 00:30:50,680
(The second brother is
enjoying the freedom...)

609
00:30:50,681 --> 00:30:52,081
(over the dizzying gorge.)

610
00:30:52,811 --> 00:30:54,151
It's going backward.

611
00:30:54,281 --> 00:30:55,521
I'll try to go forward.

612
00:30:56,751 --> 00:30:57,821
Forward...

613
00:30:59,021 --> 00:31:01,581
(It's a refreshing ride even if
he can't control the direction.)

614
00:31:06,391 --> 00:31:08,561
My shoe.

615
00:31:09,731 --> 00:31:12,431
(He's still cheerful
when his shoe is gone.)

616
00:31:13,871 --> 00:31:16,971
(His shoe was safely rescued
thanks to the safety guard.)

617
00:31:17,941 --> 00:31:19,970
(Meanwhile, the youngest
also gets ready to go.)

618
00:31:19,971 --> 00:31:21,240
Go? Here?

619
00:31:21,241 --> 00:31:23,381
Here and here?

620
00:31:24,411 --> 00:31:26,951
Here? Do I... No?

621
00:31:27,211 --> 00:31:29,051
Hand... Okay?

622
00:31:29,321 --> 00:31:31,020
- Here, here.
- Yes.

623
00:31:31,021 --> 00:31:33,091
(Endless safety checking)

624
00:31:34,251 --> 00:31:35,791
Okay. I'll get going!

625
00:31:36,421 --> 00:31:38,361
(Joon sets off as well.)

626
00:31:38,461 --> 00:31:39,591
I'll get going!

627
00:31:40,061 --> 00:31:42,561
(Bring it on, zipline!)

628
00:31:45,801 --> 00:31:48,631
(A refreshing glide over a lush forest)

629
00:31:50,171 --> 00:31:51,701
It's scary!

630
00:31:52,511 --> 00:31:54,741
(Rotating)

631
00:31:57,081 --> 00:31:58,341
It's scary!

632
00:31:59,181 --> 00:32:02,781
(A strange mix of fear and excitement)

633
00:32:06,051 --> 00:32:09,221
(Help!)

634
00:32:11,161 --> 00:32:14,191
(He couldn't land smoothly, but
he conquered the scary zipline.)

635
00:32:18,731 --> 00:32:19,771
(Exclaiming)

636
00:32:20,131 --> 00:32:21,431
It was scarier than I thought.

637
00:32:22,741 --> 00:32:24,861
It's only scary at the
beginning right before moving.

638
00:32:25,271 --> 00:32:26,370
(He's in that moment.)

639
00:32:26,371 --> 00:32:27,541
It's scary.

640
00:32:29,811 --> 00:32:30,881
Goodness...

641
00:32:31,211 --> 00:32:33,011
This is crazy.

642
00:32:34,311 --> 00:32:35,311
(Moving slowly)

643
00:32:39,451 --> 00:32:41,221
Goodness.

644
00:32:41,551 --> 00:32:44,061
This is really scary.

645
00:32:44,521 --> 00:32:46,831
Goodness.

646
00:32:46,991 --> 00:32:49,361
It's scary.

647
00:32:50,701 --> 00:32:52,061
(Laughing)

648
00:32:52,171 --> 00:32:54,170
(He's even laughing in fear.)

649
00:32:54,171 --> 00:32:55,441
It's so scary.

650
00:32:56,071 --> 00:32:59,041
(He's too scared to keep filming.)

651
00:33:00,011 --> 00:33:01,111
This is embarrassing.

652
00:33:01,911 --> 00:33:05,111
It looks like there's no net
because the net is green.

653
00:33:15,591 --> 00:33:16,921
Goodness.

654
00:33:19,161 --> 00:33:23,661
(He's only at the starting point.)

655
00:33:25,631 --> 00:33:27,701
You don't know what I'm seeing right now.

656
00:33:28,501 --> 00:33:29,871
This is what I'm seeing.

657
00:33:30,301 --> 00:33:31,501
I have to go there.

658
00:33:34,511 --> 00:33:36,411
It's just like jumping off.

659
00:33:38,141 --> 00:33:40,211
Is it tight enough?

660
00:33:41,451 --> 00:33:42,721
I'm scared.

661
00:33:44,021 --> 00:33:45,321
Come down!

662
00:33:45,991 --> 00:33:48,420
Why isn't he coming?

663
00:33:48,421 --> 00:33:50,460
It was higher than I thought.

664
00:33:50,461 --> 00:33:51,761
That's what's scary at first.

665
00:33:52,991 --> 00:33:53,991
Okay.

666
00:33:53,992 --> 00:33:55,130
(Safety check complete)

667
00:33:55,131 --> 00:33:56,131
Is it okay?

668
00:33:56,631 --> 00:33:58,161
It's so scary!

669
00:34:02,371 --> 00:34:05,070
(The eldest also begins the
flight with a frowning face.)

670
00:34:05,071 --> 00:34:06,371
No!

671
00:34:09,541 --> 00:34:11,281
He's coming.

672
00:34:11,541 --> 00:34:14,181
(Screaming)

673
00:34:14,611 --> 00:34:17,751
(His pupils are dilated with fear.)

674
00:34:18,321 --> 00:34:20,567
(The eldest soars above Iya
Valley with an endless scream.)

675
00:34:20,591 --> 00:34:22,120
We all come facing backward.

676
00:34:22,121 --> 00:34:23,190
I wanted to face forward,

677
00:34:23,191 --> 00:34:24,461
but I couldn't turn myself.

678
00:34:24,961 --> 00:34:28,161
(That's not the problem.
(Hyun Moo just wants it to end.)

679
00:34:28,591 --> 00:34:29,860
Legs. Fold the legs.

680
00:34:29,861 --> 00:34:31,000
Fold your legs.

681
00:34:31,001 --> 00:34:32,841
You'll break your legs
if you don't fold them!

682
00:34:33,501 --> 00:34:34,631
Fold your legs!

683
00:34:35,001 --> 00:34:37,161
(He goes down gloriously
with a chaotic camera angle.)

684
00:34:39,411 --> 00:34:41,141
It was like an airborne force mission.

685
00:34:43,141 --> 00:34:44,211
How was it?

686
00:34:44,811 --> 00:34:45,881
It was so scary.

687
00:34:46,181 --> 00:34:47,350
Well done.

688
00:34:47,351 --> 00:34:48,780
We have one more left. Come here.

689
00:34:48,781 --> 00:34:50,021
We have one more left.

690
00:34:50,751 --> 00:34:52,051
This is scary.

691
00:34:53,221 --> 00:34:54,720
Did I look cool coming down?

692
00:34:54,721 --> 00:34:56,160
- No.
- What? "No?"

693
00:34:56,161 --> 00:34:58,390
None of us looked cool on the zipline.

694
00:34:58,391 --> 00:34:59,791
We all came facing backward.

695
00:35:00,791 --> 00:35:02,231
We still survived.

696
00:35:02,631 --> 00:35:04,431
- Let's go.
- Let's head to the next course.

697
00:35:05,701 --> 00:35:06,901
Are you not scared now?

698
00:35:07,371 --> 00:35:09,240
- I felt...
- I wasn't scared before, either.

699
00:35:09,241 --> 00:35:11,361
I wasn't scared because I
knew what it would be like.

700
00:35:14,771 --> 00:35:16,581
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

701
00:35:17,211 --> 00:35:18,480
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

702
00:35:18,481 --> 00:35:20,751
Look at him. He's a paratrooper.

703
00:35:21,211 --> 00:35:22,720
He looks cool.

704
00:35:22,721 --> 00:35:23,881
He does.

705
00:35:26,221 --> 00:35:27,421
Where is the drone?

706
00:35:29,091 --> 00:35:31,560
That one?

707
00:35:31,561 --> 00:35:33,831
(This time, he even spots
the drone and says hello.)

708
00:35:34,361 --> 00:35:36,101
(He just envies him.)

709
00:35:36,861 --> 00:35:38,261
Let's face forward now.

710
00:35:48,741 --> 00:35:50,540
- I'll get going.
- I'll take a cool video of you.

711
00:35:50,541 --> 00:35:52,581
- I should try to look cool.
- Say hello.

712
00:35:53,851 --> 00:35:56,481
(I'll make sure to look cool this time.)

713
00:35:58,751 --> 00:36:01,351
(He looks more relaxed.)

714
00:36:02,151 --> 00:36:05,060
(He can experience the
true joy of the zipline...)

715
00:36:05,061 --> 00:36:07,961
(now that he's overcome his fear.)

716
00:36:08,261 --> 00:36:09,261
Nice.

717
00:36:16,901 --> 00:36:17,971
Okay.

718
00:36:18,201 --> 00:36:20,771
(The youngest feels proud of
himself for overcoming his fear.)

719
00:36:21,271 --> 00:36:23,481
(Meanwhile, the eldest...)

720
00:36:24,311 --> 00:36:26,511
(He's still afraid of the zipline.)

721
00:36:26,951 --> 00:36:28,781
No!

722
00:36:31,121 --> 00:36:32,591
(Screaming)

723
00:36:33,591 --> 00:36:35,021
My foot touched a tree!

724
00:36:37,691 --> 00:36:39,661
- He took off right away.
- Yes.

725
00:36:40,631 --> 00:36:41,731
It wouldn't be scary now.

726
00:36:42,801 --> 00:36:45,131
(No, it's scary.)

727
00:36:45,801 --> 00:36:48,431
Drone!

728
00:36:48,801 --> 00:36:50,341
Drone!

729
00:36:50,441 --> 00:36:53,201
(It looks like he found the second
sibling waving at the drone cool.)

730
00:36:55,111 --> 00:36:57,511
(But the eldest only looks
like he's signalling for help.)

731
00:37:01,581 --> 00:37:02,751
Raise your legs.

732
00:37:04,051 --> 00:37:05,580
(He lands with his whole body again.)

733
00:37:05,581 --> 00:37:07,921
Goodness.

734
00:37:08,791 --> 00:37:11,161
You're in a mess.

735
00:37:11,621 --> 00:37:13,460
- It's still fun.
- It was fun.

736
00:37:13,461 --> 00:37:15,331
- We had fun.
- Thank you.

737
00:37:18,961 --> 00:37:20,200
Do you want to take a shower?

738
00:37:20,201 --> 00:37:21,300
- Yes.
- I really want to take a shower.

739
00:37:21,301 --> 00:37:22,471
- It's...
- I need a shower.

740
00:37:22,801 --> 00:37:25,040
You'd feel grossed out. How
long have you worn that outfit?

741
00:37:25,041 --> 00:37:26,071
Two days?

742
00:37:26,441 --> 00:37:27,971
We're soaked in sweat.

743
00:37:29,281 --> 00:37:30,511
I'll give you some options.

744
00:37:30,941 --> 00:37:32,081
Option one.

745
00:37:32,881 --> 00:37:34,450
Entering cold water.

746
00:37:34,451 --> 00:37:35,880
Cold water? It's option one for sure.

747
00:37:35,881 --> 00:37:36,921
Option two.

748
00:37:37,551 --> 00:37:39,550
Entering water hotter than this weather.

749
00:37:39,551 --> 00:37:41,191
Isn't option one the best then?

750
00:37:41,351 --> 00:37:43,421
Option 1. But you want option 2, right?

751
00:37:43,821 --> 00:37:44,891
Really?

752
00:37:46,031 --> 00:37:48,471
We're already sweating. You
still want to get into hot water?

753
00:37:48,931 --> 00:37:51,831
If we enter cold water,

754
00:37:52,571 --> 00:37:56,201
we'll miss out on a must-visit place here.

755
00:37:57,671 --> 00:37:59,041
The answer was already decided.

756
00:38:00,371 --> 00:38:01,770
(They'll be overcoming the heat with heat.)

757
00:38:01,771 --> 00:38:04,011
- It's hot.
- It's so hot.

758
00:38:11,621 --> 00:38:15,861
(Zipline, hot spring)

759
00:38:17,021 --> 00:38:20,791
(Hotel)

760
00:38:21,961 --> 00:38:24,301
Let's go. Move!

761
00:38:25,201 --> 00:38:28,070
I ignored your opinions...

762
00:38:28,071 --> 00:38:29,701
and came to the place with hot water.

763
00:38:30,571 --> 00:38:32,641
He ignored it.

764
00:38:33,111 --> 00:38:34,571
I had to.

765
00:38:34,871 --> 00:38:36,180
This is an amazing place.

766
00:38:36,181 --> 00:38:37,680
Even if you don't lodge here,

767
00:38:37,681 --> 00:38:39,780
you can pay around 12 dollars...

768
00:38:39,781 --> 00:38:41,951
to enter the hot spring.

769
00:38:43,551 --> 00:38:46,591
(Japan, the country of hot springs,
with around 2,900 hot spring towns)

770
00:38:47,851 --> 00:38:49,790
(This place is known
for its traditional ryokan...)

771
00:38:49,791 --> 00:38:51,721
(and breathtaking scenery.)

772
00:38:53,561 --> 00:38:57,261
(Iya hot spring town,
Tokushima's top hot spring location)

773
00:38:58,261 --> 00:39:00,430
(A place where you can enjoy
the beauty of one of Japan's...)

774
00:39:00,431 --> 00:39:03,341
(top 3 scenic spots
and relaxing hot springs)

775
00:39:04,671 --> 00:39:06,470
- Do we have to make a reservation?
- Yes.

776
00:39:06,471 --> 00:39:09,311
(The three brothers enter
the hotel with excitement.)

777
00:39:10,011 --> 00:39:11,411
They're guests checking in.

778
00:39:12,851 --> 00:39:13,951
What's that?

779
00:39:14,281 --> 00:39:15,651
Amazing.

780
00:39:15,951 --> 00:39:17,350
Hong Kong, Asia.

781
00:39:17,351 --> 00:39:19,520
- Taiwanese people love this place.
- They're all from Taiwan.

782
00:39:19,521 --> 00:39:21,121
There are people from Singapore as well.

783
