1044
00:52:15,261 --> 00:52:16,530
It'd be insane at night.

1045
00:52:16,531 --> 00:52:17,601
I bet some of them move.

1046
00:52:18,061 --> 00:52:19,061
(Screaming)

1047
00:52:19,062 --> 00:52:20,070
What on earth?

1048
00:52:20,071 --> 00:52:22,231
This is creepy.

1049
00:52:22,701 --> 00:52:24,871
(This village is...)

1050
00:52:27,471 --> 00:52:29,370
(A village with more
scarecrows than people, )

1051
00:52:29,371 --> 00:52:31,131
(Nagoro, Miyoshi City,
Tokushima Prefecture)

1052
00:52:31,211 --> 00:52:35,911
(Now a must-visit even for
horror fans from overseas)

1053
00:52:36,081 --> 00:52:39,651
(They say an elderly woman
makes the scarecrows all by herself.)

1054
00:52:45,161 --> 00:52:47,291
Does nobody live here anymore?

1055
00:52:47,631 --> 00:52:48,761
No one lives here?

1056
00:52:50,061 --> 00:52:51,201
There's no one here.

1057
00:52:53,101 --> 00:52:54,771
Why did everyone leave?

1058
00:53:01,271 --> 00:53:03,880
I think someone still lives in that house.

1059
00:53:03,881 --> 00:53:04,911
Or maybe not?

1060
00:53:05,181 --> 00:53:08,081
(Nam Gil says he sees someone.)

1061
00:53:08,751 --> 00:53:09,951
Oh, my.

1062
00:53:11,451 --> 00:53:13,351
Someone's working over here.

1063
00:53:14,051 --> 00:53:15,891
Someone's working over here.

1064
00:53:17,261 --> 00:53:18,390
(He seems to have spotted something.)

1065
00:53:18,391 --> 00:53:19,891
- Where?
- Here?

1066
00:53:21,461 --> 00:53:22,791
You're right.

1067
00:53:23,291 --> 00:53:25,061
Hyun Moo!

1068
00:53:25,931 --> 00:53:28,730
- What did you see?
- I think the owner's over there.

1069
00:53:28,731 --> 00:53:30,671
They're working.

1070
00:53:31,141 --> 00:53:32,341
Right?

1071
00:53:32,471 --> 00:53:34,311
- That's not a scarecrow, right?
- I guess so.

1072
00:53:34,571 --> 00:53:35,971
It must be a person, right?

1073
00:53:38,781 --> 00:53:41,450
(At this point, )

1074
00:53:41,451 --> 00:53:44,151
(they can't tell who's human
and who's a scarecrow.)

1075
00:53:46,651 --> 00:53:48,421
- Excuse me.
- Excuse me.

1076
00:53:48,591 --> 00:53:50,720
- Hello.
- Hello.

1077
00:53:50,721 --> 00:53:53,161
(Is she real?)

1078
00:53:55,061 --> 00:53:57,000
(She springs to her feet.)

1079
00:53:57,001 --> 00:53:58,061
Hello.

1080
00:53:58,261 --> 00:54:00,001
Are you here all by yourself?

1081
00:54:00,501 --> 00:54:01,547
I'm here with the scarecrows.

1082
00:54:01,571 --> 00:54:03,671
With the scarecrows... I see.

1083
00:54:04,301 --> 00:54:06,940
- You are amazing. They are great.
- Thank you.

1084
00:54:06,941 --> 00:54:08,141
Yes.

1085
00:54:08,341 --> 00:54:11,381
Did you make...

1086
00:54:12,281 --> 00:54:13,750
all of these by yourself?

1087
00:54:13,751 --> 00:54:14,881
Yes, I did.

1088
00:54:16,981 --> 00:54:18,380
She made all these by herself.

1089
00:54:18,381 --> 00:54:19,580
Right.

1090
00:54:19,581 --> 00:54:21,821
- She made all of them, right?
- That's right.

1091
00:54:24,621 --> 00:54:26,930
How long have you been making them?

1092
00:54:26,931 --> 00:54:29,160
For about 22 years.

1093
00:54:29,161 --> 00:54:30,161
22 years?

1094
00:54:30,162 --> 00:54:32,461
(Scarecrows she's made on
her own over the past 22 years)

1095
00:54:32,601 --> 00:54:34,370
This is...

1096
00:54:34,371 --> 00:54:37,471
Nagoro Scarecrow Village in Miyoshi City.

1097
00:54:38,141 --> 00:54:39,970
(Tsukimi Ayano, the mother of scarecrows)

1098
00:54:39,971 --> 00:54:42,071
(Age 77)

1099
00:54:42,411 --> 00:54:45,441
There are about 360 scarecrows here now.

1100
00:54:46,711 --> 00:54:48,950
(Decorating every corner of the village...)

1101
00:54:48,951 --> 00:54:51,951
(are hundreds of scarecrows.)

1102
00:54:55,421 --> 00:54:57,561
(Welcome!)

1103
00:54:57,991 --> 00:55:00,991
(Along the roads and by houses, )

1104
00:55:01,431 --> 00:55:06,101
(scarecrows in all shapes and
sizes bring the whole village to life.)

1105
00:55:06,531 --> 00:55:08,830
There were once about 300 people...

1106
00:55:08,831 --> 00:55:10,871
living in this village.

1107
00:55:11,071 --> 00:55:14,071
(A once-lively village
with around 300 residents)

1108
00:55:14,811 --> 00:55:19,681
(The population dwindled
to just 20 residents.)

1109
00:55:20,041 --> 00:55:23,821
(Scarecrows made to fill the void)

1110
00:55:24,181 --> 00:55:26,750
All these scarecrow dolls...

1111
00:55:26,751 --> 00:55:28,491
are like my children, my family.

1112
00:55:30,661 --> 00:55:32,720
(I made this one.)

1113
00:55:32,721 --> 00:55:34,930
(To her, they're more than dolls.)

1114
00:55:34,931 --> 00:55:36,961
(Each one is like a
child she lovingly raised.)

1115
00:55:37,561 --> 00:55:39,760
They're stuffed with newspaper,

1116
00:55:39,761 --> 00:55:42,700
so they last only about two years.

1117
00:55:42,701 --> 00:55:47,371
So I dress them in old clothes.

1118
00:55:47,941 --> 00:55:51,011
(Made one by one with the
care she'd give her own children)

1119
00:55:51,341 --> 00:55:52,981
- You're amazing.
- You're incredible.

1120
00:55:53,411 --> 00:55:55,550
We're from Korea.

1121
00:55:55,551 --> 00:55:57,020
We're filming a TV show.

1122
00:55:57,021 --> 00:55:58,520
Which of you is famous?

1123
00:55:58,521 --> 00:56:02,190
He's the most famous one. He's an actor.

1124
00:56:02,191 --> 00:56:04,790
An actor? I don't know much
about Korean celebrities.

1125
00:56:04,791 --> 00:56:06,260
That's okay.

1126
00:56:06,261 --> 00:56:07,390
- Handsome.
- Handsome.

1127
00:56:07,391 --> 00:56:08,660
- You're handsome.
- You're handsome.

1128
00:56:08,661 --> 00:56:09,961
Thank you.

1129
00:56:10,231 --> 00:56:11,500
He's an idol.

1130
00:56:11,501 --> 00:56:12,660
(Am I handsome, too?)

1131
00:56:12,661 --> 00:56:14,371
He's a K-pop idol.

1132
00:56:14,771 --> 00:56:15,930
You're cute.

1133
00:56:15,931 --> 00:56:19,901
(The trio's fan meeting
in a mountain village)

1134
00:56:20,211 --> 00:56:22,141
(What handsome young men!)

1135
00:56:22,241 --> 00:56:24,011
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1136
00:56:26,881 --> 00:56:29,751
She seemed a bit curt at
first, so I was a little scared.

1137
00:56:30,551 --> 00:56:32,581
Maybe she hasn't talked
to anyone in a while.

1138
00:56:32,681 --> 00:56:33,820
- Right.
- Right?

1139
00:56:33,821 --> 00:56:36,190
But thanks to the scarecrows she made,

1140
00:56:36,191 --> 00:56:38,091
tourists come here,

1141
00:56:38,321 --> 00:56:41,260
and the elderly residents
get to see people.

1142
00:56:41,261 --> 00:56:43,160
People wouldn't have
come without the scarecrows.

1143
00:56:43,161 --> 00:56:45,261
Right. That's incredible.

1144
00:56:47,331 --> 00:56:48,630
So this is where she makes them.

1145
00:56:48,631 --> 00:56:49,930
She makes them here...

1146
00:56:49,931 --> 00:56:51,971
This is her art studio.

1147
00:56:52,601 --> 00:56:54,411
They're cute.

1148
00:56:58,481 --> 00:56:59,741
This is where she makes them.

1149
00:57:00,181 --> 00:57:01,381
There are so many inside.

1150
00:57:02,051 --> 00:57:03,381
This is insane.

1151
00:57:04,251 --> 00:57:05,751
She's an incredible woman.

1152
00:57:07,121 --> 00:57:10,051
- She really is amazing.
- It's different here.

1153
00:57:10,461 --> 00:57:14,060
(Her children, gathered together)

1154
00:57:14,061 --> 00:57:16,331
- She's an artist.
- She is.

1155
00:57:17,031 --> 00:57:19,501
- I thought she'd made about ten.
- Yes.

1156
00:57:19,601 --> 00:57:20,730
I thought she was just dabbling,

1157
00:57:20,731 --> 00:57:22,971
but she's created a whole village.

1158
00:57:23,231 --> 00:57:25,841
- This is amazing.
- No wonder it took 22 years.

1159
00:57:28,641 --> 00:57:29,971
Look over there.

1160
00:57:30,071 --> 00:57:31,441
- At the far end.
- Yes.

1161
00:57:31,641 --> 00:57:33,410
That's an elementary school.

1162
00:57:33,411 --> 00:57:35,051
This is insane.

1163
00:57:35,551 --> 00:57:39,151
(Further inside the village, )

1164
00:57:39,721 --> 00:57:42,851
(there is an old elementary school.)

1165
00:57:43,051 --> 00:57:45,860
(Scarecrow Elementary School)

1166
00:57:45,861 --> 00:57:47,031
Let's go, then.

1167
00:57:48,031 --> 00:57:50,431
This must be how they got to school.

1168
00:57:51,131 --> 00:57:54,071
Imagine having a mountain
stream right in front of your school.

1169
00:57:54,501 --> 00:57:55,601
Goodness.

1170
00:57:57,171 --> 00:57:58,571
It's so close to nature.

1171
00:58:00,171 --> 00:58:01,471
It must've been a lovely school.

1172
00:58:03,011 --> 00:58:04,781
- There's no one here.
- What's that?

1173
00:58:06,081 --> 00:58:07,251
That startled me.

1174
00:58:07,351 --> 00:58:08,711
Hi, kids!

1175
00:58:09,411 --> 00:58:11,250
- The head hall monitor.
- A hall monitor?

1176
00:58:11,251 --> 00:58:13,950
They're hall monitors
holding warning lights.

1177
00:58:13,951 --> 00:58:15,351
They're so cute.

1178
00:58:16,551 --> 00:58:17,861
And this is the schoolyard.

1179
00:58:18,491 --> 00:58:20,611
That painting must be from
back when it was a school.

1180
00:58:22,831 --> 00:58:24,931
(Transfer students?)

1181
00:58:28,201 --> 00:58:29,571
Where did Nam Gil go this time?

1182
00:58:30,771 --> 00:58:33,441
(The eldest and youngest look
away, and Nam Gil disappears.)

1183
00:58:35,441 --> 00:58:36,941
- Hey!
- What?

1184
00:58:37,981 --> 00:58:40,481
(Nam Gil's urgent voice
rings out from somewhere.)

1185
00:58:40,981 --> 00:58:42,450
(A sharp scream from Nam Gil)

1186
00:58:42,451 --> 00:58:44,051
(What on earth happened to Nam Gil?)

1187
00:58:44,581 --> 00:58:46,281
(Moments earlier)

1188
00:58:48,051 --> 00:58:50,821
(Nam Gil spots something.)

1189
00:58:52,461 --> 00:58:54,661
(As if in a trance, he runs off...)

1190
00:58:59,501 --> 00:59:02,001
(and vanishes into the building.)

1191
00:59:02,431 --> 00:59:05,301
(Nam Gil's location)

1192
00:59:09,011 --> 00:59:10,481
Hi, kids!

1193
00:59:14,681 --> 00:59:15,811
My gosh!

1194
00:59:18,781 --> 00:59:19,850
Look at this.

1195
00:59:19,851 --> 00:59:21,050
(Looking grave)

1196
00:59:21,051 --> 00:59:23,390
Coming in alone gives
you serious goosebumps.

1197
00:59:23,391 --> 00:59:24,920
I got goosebumps all over.

1198
00:59:24,921 --> 00:59:25,990
- Hey.
- What?

1199
00:59:25,991 --> 00:59:27,091
Where are you going?

1200
00:59:27,491 --> 00:59:28,491
Can we go in?

1201
00:59:28,492 --> 00:59:29,812
(What on earth did Nam Gil find?)

1202
00:59:31,131 --> 00:59:32,661
It'd be super scary at night.

1203
00:59:32,761 --> 00:59:34,830
- It'd be insane at night.
- I bet some of them move.

1204
00:59:34,831 --> 00:59:36,471
This is as late as I'd dare come.

1205
00:59:36,931 --> 00:59:40,341
Try going in alone. I
got serious goosebumps.

1206
00:59:40,711 --> 00:59:41,711
Okay.

1207
00:59:44,941 --> 00:59:47,550
(Frozen)

1208
00:59:47,551 --> 00:59:49,581
It feels...

1209
00:59:50,821 --> 00:59:52,821
I'm scared.

1210
00:59:54,451 --> 00:59:55,551
Scary.

1211
01:00:03,931 --> 01:00:04,931
No way!

1212
01:00:04,932 --> 01:00:06,131
Right?

1213
01:00:07,701 --> 01:00:08,871
No way!

1214
01:00:09,931 --> 01:00:11,341
No way!

1215
01:00:11,801 --> 01:00:17,081
(A gym full of scarecrows
instead of people)

1216
01:00:23,651 --> 01:00:26,881
I was so startled when
I first came in alone.

1217
01:00:27,521 --> 01:00:29,251
My goodness.

1218
01:00:30,321 --> 01:00:31,561
Look at this.

1219
01:00:32,391 --> 01:00:33,961
Hello.

1220
01:00:35,161 --> 01:00:36,161
Goodness.

1221
01:00:36,162 --> 01:00:38,660
(Hundreds of eyes stare back in silence.)

1222
01:00:38,661 --> 01:00:41,001
It's so impressive and artistic...

1223
01:00:41,071 --> 01:00:42,331
- Right?
- My gosh.

1224
01:00:43,601 --> 01:00:48,041
(A gym once bustling with villagers)

1225
01:00:49,511 --> 01:00:53,311
(Scarecrows now fill the
space they left behind.)

1226
01:00:53,481 --> 01:00:54,811
It's a school sports day.

1227
01:00:55,011 --> 01:00:58,020
Parents and grandmothers
came for the sports day.

1228
01:00:58,021 --> 01:00:59,221
Here's a tug-of-war.

1229
01:00:59,451 --> 01:01:01,551
She even made a tug-of-war scene.

1230
01:01:03,051 --> 01:01:05,721
Each one must've taken so much hard work.

1231
01:01:12,261 --> 01:01:15,531
(The villagers' cheers
that would've filled the gym)

1232
01:01:17,471 --> 01:01:20,300
Cosmos Festival.
They're getting ready for it.

1233
01:01:20,301 --> 01:01:22,821
(An autumn festival they enjoyed
as the cosmos flowers bloomed)

1234
01:01:23,341 --> 01:01:27,480
(Awa Odori dancing that
brought the festival nights to life)

1235
01:01:27,481 --> 01:01:28,811
There are so many.

1236
01:01:29,251 --> 01:01:32,951
She didn't just take old
scarecrows apart and remodel them.

1237
01:01:33,421 --> 01:01:35,741
- They're all different.
- She made them all from scratch.

1238
01:01:35,891 --> 01:01:38,891
- That's why it took so long.
- This really is incredible.

1239
01:01:40,631 --> 01:01:44,701
(Though people left
the village one by one, )

1240
01:01:47,031 --> 01:01:51,141
(the scarecrows wait for
someone to visit again.)

1241
01:01:51,801 --> 01:01:54,110
As long as I'm healthy,

1242
01:01:54,111 --> 01:01:56,510
I'll keep making these scarecrows,

1243
01:01:56,511 --> 01:02:00,011
so I hope lots of people visit.

1244
01:02:00,141 --> 01:02:01,710
Please come and see them.

1245
01:02:01,711 --> 01:02:04,481
(Please come and see them.)

1246
01:02:06,681 --> 01:02:08,121
I'm tired.

1247
01:02:10,691 --> 01:02:12,661
The mountains here are so high.

1248
01:02:12,991 --> 01:02:15,061
It feels like we're the
last people left on Earth.

1249
01:02:16,391 --> 01:02:19,061
Did something just run past on the right?

1250
01:02:21,131 --> 01:02:23,000
Something ran past. It
looked like a wild boar.

1251
01:02:23,001 --> 01:02:25,217
(Something like a wild boar
ran by, just as Hyun Moo said.)

1252
01:02:25,241 --> 01:02:26,970
It's a raccoon dog.

1253
01:02:26,971 --> 01:02:29,141
(Wild locals pop up everywhere they go.)

1254
01:02:29,371 --> 01:02:30,580
It's a deer.

1255
01:02:30,581 --> 01:02:31,581
- My gosh.
- My gosh.

1256
01:02:31,581 --> 01:02:32,581
My gosh.

1257
01:02:32,582 --> 01:02:33,841
Bambi.

1258
01:02:35,511 --> 01:02:36,880
(The unfazed deer greets
them with a glance, then leaves.)

1259
01:02:36,881 --> 01:02:38,121
There's a deer.

1260
01:02:38,981 --> 01:02:40,750
We might even see a bear here!

1261
01:02:40,751 --> 01:02:42,120
This is crazy.

1262
01:02:42,121 --> 01:02:44,020
But bears could easily turn up here.

1263
01:02:44,021 --> 01:02:46,660
- Japan has so many bears.
- So many.

1264
01:02:46,661 --> 01:02:48,530
That's right.

1265
01:02:48,531 --> 01:02:50,051
You hear about bears attacking people.

1266
01:02:50,131 --> 01:02:56,331
(Bear sightings are
currently a hot topic in Japan.)

1267
01:02:56,501 --> 01:02:58,140
- I'm hungry.
- What are we eating?

1268
01:02:58,141 --> 01:03:00,170
I've got an amazing
dinner lined up for us, too.

1269
01:03:00,171 --> 01:03:01,541
My gosh, that sounds delicious.

1270
01:03:02,771 --> 01:03:04,710
It's amazing there are houses here.

1271
01:03:04,711 --> 01:03:06,757
(A lone building at the end of a
seemingly endless mountain road?)

1272
01:03:06,781 --> 01:03:08,181
What's this?

1273
01:03:08,681 --> 01:03:09,951
Is this a restaurant?

1274
01:03:10,781 --> 01:03:15,051
(Scarecrow Village to restaurant)

1275
01:03:16,751 --> 01:03:18,620
My gosh, there's a restaurant here?

1276
01:03:18,621 --> 01:03:19,621
Goodness, what is this place?

1277
01:03:19,622 --> 01:03:21,060
My gosh, this place is really...

1278
01:03:21,061 --> 01:03:23,161
Even the locals might
not know about this place.

1279
01:03:25,131 --> 01:03:27,731
They sell yakitori. I can smell it.

1280
01:03:29,971 --> 01:03:33,200
(What seems to be a yakitori
place on a quiet mountain road)

1281
01:03:33,201 --> 01:03:34,371
- My gosh.
- It must be good.

1282
01:03:35,271 --> 01:03:38,511
This is incredible. Is
this really a restaurant?

1283
01:03:42,011 --> 01:03:43,611
There are people here.

1284
01:03:45,221 --> 01:03:46,281
Hello.

1285
01:03:49,291 --> 01:03:52,520
Are you open right now?

1286
01:03:52,521 --> 01:03:54,531
- We're open.
- You are?

1287
01:03:55,061 --> 01:03:56,990
- How many in your party? Three.
- Three.

1288
01:03:56,991 --> 01:03:58,401
Yes, right this way.

1289
01:03:58,501 --> 01:03:59,501
What a relief.

1290
01:04:12,241 --> 01:04:14,510
Goodness, they have so many dishes.

1291
01:04:14,511 --> 01:04:17,450
- They have omurice, fried rice...
- They all look good.

1292
01:04:17,451 --> 01:04:19,280
My gosh, look at this!

1293
01:04:19,281 --> 01:04:21,121
Goodness, there's so much here.

1294
01:04:22,221 --> 01:04:24,260
They have tsukune, too.
You know tsukune, right?

1295
01:04:24,261 --> 01:04:25,320
What's tsukune?

1296
01:04:25,321 --> 01:04:27,221
It's like a chicken meatball.

1297
01:04:27,731 --> 01:04:29,067
The one at the top
that looks like a hot dog.

1298
01:04:29,091 --> 01:04:30,800
- My gosh.
- I like chicken...

1299
01:04:30,801 --> 01:04:32,801
You really know everything.

1300
